on form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139535931 true] [17592186375125 1113 #uuid "28d32302-16b0-5cdc-a69e-754fd94318a8" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375125 1145 "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=-1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-1-2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1-2y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375126 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375127 13194139535931 true] [17592186375126 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375128 13194139535931 true] [17592186375126 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375129 13194139535931 true] [17592186375126 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375130 13194139535931 true] [17592186375126 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375131 13194139535931 true] [17592186375126 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535931 true] [17592186375126 1041 "selection" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375126 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375127 13194139535931 true] [17592186375126 1110 #uuid "38efa2d1-90b7-5a8e-b8f2-28ae7d0ce4a9" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375127 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375127 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535931 true] [17592186375127 1111 #uuid "67ce3d47-3a84-5e17-90b5-808e763e7600" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375128 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375128 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535931 true] [17592186375128 1111 #uuid "75c1aea2-3b43-5433-afdd-3342b9b8199d" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375129 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375129 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535931 true] [17592186375129 1111 #uuid "f19c4b5d-373e-56d0-a2d5-a2f69be406d4" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375130 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375130 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535931 true] [17592186375130 1111 #uuid "e9026196-05ec-500e-9e73-bcb561d459d6" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375131 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375131 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535931 true] [17592186375131 1111 #uuid "e3cd479c-433f-5017-89d7-3a080859c4cc" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375132 1017 #edb/ref 17592186375133 13194139535931 true] [17592186375132 1089 "q-73750" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375132 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535931 true] [17592186375132 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=4 \\\\ -3x+6y=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." 13194139535931 true] [17592186375132 1113 #uuid "79d64547-fc54-5cd3-a6ec-b00c0e085729" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375132 1145 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -12\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=4 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-2y=4.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=4+2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375133 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375134 13194139535931 true] [17592186375133 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375135 13194139535931 true] [17592186375133 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375136 13194139535931 true] [17592186375133 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375137 13194139535931 true] [17592186375133 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375138 13194139535931 true] [17592186375133 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535931 true] [17592186375133 1041 "selection" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375133 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375134 13194139535931 true] [17592186375133 1110 #uuid "834515f8-6272-5827-bfac-7bf41c342fd2" 13194139535931 true] [17592186375134 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\b